WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.799
A real exchange rate, measured as its distance from purchasing

00:03.899 --> 00:07.698
power parity. Forty years of quarterly data. The Dickey Fuller

00:07.798 --> 00:10.843
test cannot reject a unit root, and on series like

00:10.943 --> 00:13.170
this one it fails four times in five.

00:13.766 --> 00:17.224
Yet the series never escapes a narrow corridor. A random walk

00:17.324 --> 00:20.432
would have wandered off long ago. How can both be true?

00:21.500 --> 00:24.393
The answer is a model whose rule changes with

00:24.493 --> 00:27.852
the state of the series: a threshold autoregression.

00:28.933 --> 00:33.398
Picture a ball in a valley. Its position is the deviation from

00:33.498 --> 00:37.742
parity. Near parity the floor is not a bowl: it is slightly

00:37.842 --> 00:44.074
domed. Transaction costs make arbitrage unprofitable, nothing pulls the ball back, and

00:44.174 --> 00:48.639
it rolls away from the centre. Beyond the band edges, plus and

00:48.739 --> 00:53.573
minus gamma, the walls rise: arbitrage pays, and the ball is pushed

00:53.673 --> 00:57.254
back. Below, its path leaves a trail through time.

00:57.333 --> 01:02.019
In equations, the threshold variable is the size of the last deviation.

01:02.119 --> 01:06.468
Inside the band, rho one is one point zero six: locally explosive.

01:06.568 --> 01:10.918
Outside, rho two is zero point nine two: mean reverting. The trail

01:11.018 --> 01:13.951
is yellow on the floor and teal on the walls.

01:14.033 --> 01:19.188
Here is the surprise. One regime is explosive, yet the process is globally

01:19.288 --> 01:25.082
stationary. The switch is endogenous: the explosive regime pushes the series out of

01:25.182 --> 01:29.697
itself, into the regime that pulls it back. And a unit root test,

01:29.797 --> 01:33.603
which fits one line to both, sees only the persistence.

01:35.000 --> 01:38.588
How do we find gamma from data? Fix a candidate gamma and

01:38.688 --> 01:42.471
the model is linear: split the points at gamma and run least

01:42.571 --> 01:47.325
squares on each side. Record the residual variance, then slide gamma along,

01:47.425 --> 01:50.625
keeping fifteen percent of the data in each regime.

01:51.200 --> 01:55.767
Between two neighbouring observations nothing changes, so the objective is

01:55.867 --> 01:58.984
a staircase: flat, then a jump each time the cursor

01:59.084 --> 02:02.202
crosses a data point. Gamma hat is the lowest step.

02:02.300 --> 02:06.225
Drop a ball on the staircase and it settles there, close to

02:06.325 --> 02:09.978
the true value, zero. Because the dip is a cliff, not a

02:10.078 --> 02:14.345
gentle slope, gamma hat converges at rate T, faster than root T,

02:14.445 --> 02:18.030
and we may treat it as known when we study the slopes.

02:19.100 --> 02:23.241
So: a threshold autoregression lets the rule depend on the state.

02:23.341 --> 02:27.547
Persistence inside the band and reversion outside it give a series

02:27.647 --> 02:30.745
that looks like a random walk and is not one. And

02:30.845 --> 02:34.595
the threshold is found at the lowest step of the staircase.
